<section class="panel rules-page"><h1>Rules of the First Realm</h1><p>Kingdom Come is a multiplayer alpha inspired by Kingdoms Live. Our catalog and numerical rules are reconstructed, not recovered original server formulas.</p><h2>Quest, equip, invest</h2><p>Explore eleven regions with quests and equipment through level 50, then work toward the Worldroot Bastion at level 55. Mana runs repeatable quests. Equipment requirements stay owned; discoveries open later routes. Each army member automatically uses at most one weapon, one armor item and one spell; attack and defense choose different best items. Sales refund half the recorded paid cost per copy, rounded down.</p><h2>Resources and skills</h2><p>Health starts at 100, Mana at 20 and Spirit at 3. Recover 10 Health every 3 minutes, 1 Mana every 5 minutes and 1 Spirit every 2 minutes. Level-ups restore resources. One skill point adds 1 Mana or 10 Health; two add 1 Spirit. One point buys one Attack or Defense rating: +1% to the relevant army power, capped at 25 ratings each. Existing allocations remain unchanged. These training rules are reconstructed. Level milestones, ten quests and your first attacking victory award additional points.</p><h2>Land and upkeep</h2><p>Property pays every full 60 minutes after purchase, including offline hours. Each additional property of the same type costs 10% more. Existing holdings keep their saved rates. All owned upkeep equipment accrues maintenance while funded. A reserve and carried gold pay it after due Land income; no passive income is required to buy equipment.</p><p>If funds run out, upkeep equipment pauses, free gear remains usable and further charges stop. Arrears never exceed one hourly bill at suspension. Resume pays arrears and reserves one hour. No equipment is destroyed. Selling gear returns reserve above the new hourly bill; recorded arrears remain. The gold header shows Land income minus property upkeep and currently active equipment upkeep; paused gear is excluded.</p><h2>Rivals</h2><p>Attack uses 1 Spirit. The attacker needs 20 Health; the defender needs positive Health. Attack Again is available in your saved report after the existing 10-second cooldown. A defeated, zero-Health opponent must recover before another attack. Similar-level rivals are eligible. Gold moves between players, with capped loot. At most three initiated encounters per rival in 24 hours can award gold/XP.</p><p>Temporary rivals never initiate attacks. Bot encounters can award gold/XP at most once per rival and six times total per rolling 24 hours; later practice still spends Spirit and causes damage.</p><h2>Your army</h2><p>You, accepted allies and retained militia share an active army limit that grows with level. Excess recruits stay owned. Each leader equips their own force. Calling specializations are modest: Freeblade has +4% attack, −2% defense and 10% shorter Spirit recovery intervals; Warden has +4% defense, −2% attack and 10% shorter Health intervals; Spellward has −2% attack/defense and 10% shorter Mana intervals. First change is free; further changes cost 100 gold, at most once per 24 hours.</p><p>Recruit shows your persistent invitation code. An invitation changes neither army until its recipient accepts. You can reject or cancel pending invitations. Codes do not authenticate accounts; keep your password private. New invitations are limited to <%= community.army.invitationsPerDay %> per day, <%= community.army.invitationCooldownSeconds %> seconds apart, with a 24-hour same-pair cooldown.</p><h2>Realm community</h2><p>Home offers All, Battles, Comments and Broadcasts. Profile comments are public and share the same records as the Home Comments feed. Comments allow <%= community.social.commentCharacters %> characters, one every <%= community.social.commentCooldownSeconds %> seconds, up to <%= community.social.commentsPerDay %> per rolling day. Broadcasts allow <%= community.social.broadcastCharacters %> characters, one every <%= community.social.broadcastCooldownSeconds %> seconds, up to <%= community.social.broadcastsPerDay %> per day; reach level 2 and finish three quests first.</p><p>Social posts give no gold or XP. Remove your own messages, hide unwanted comments on your profile or Report inappropriate content. Operators review reports and may hide messages or restrict posting. Hidden/deleted records remain for moderation audit. Battle reports stay private to their combatants. Temporary rivals never post comments or broadcasts.</p><p>Health, Mana and Spirit recover automatically. A separate bank and paid healing service are not implemented in this alpha. Settings provides account Sign Out; Profile retains your skills, inventory, property holdings and current income.</p><h2>Bounty List</h2><p>Fund an eligible human rival’s bounty with carried gold plus a 10% fee. Another eligible hunter claims escrow by winning an attacking battle. One active bounty per target; expiry after 24 hours; cancellation after one hour. Refunds return principal, not fees. Daily and pair limits apply; allies, sponsors and temporary rivals cannot claim. <a href="/game/bounties">Read all limits on the Bounty List.</a></p><p>Active rulesets: <strong><%= alpha.id %></strong>, <strong><%= strategy.id %></strong>, <strong><%= community.id %></strong>. Resources, purchases, sales, combat and payments are decided by the server.</p><a class="button button-outline" href="<%= state?'/game/home':'/login' %>">Return to realm</a></section>
